# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
from fams import *
F = 'ighacked'
page('instagram-hacked-two-factor-turned-on-by-hacker', F, 'Instagram Hacked, Hacker Turned On Two-Factor',
 'A hacker enabled two-factor authentication on your Instagram account and you cannot log in? Why it blocks you and which recovery routes still apply.',
 'Hacker turned on two-factor on your Instagram?', 'Hacker enabled two-factor',
 'Two-factor is a good lock, which is the problem when the wrong person holds the key. Here is how to approach it.',
 'When a hacker enables two-factor authentication, the codes go to their phone, so your password alone no longer works. Do not keep guessing. Use the hacked-account recovery flow and its video selfie, check the original email for a revert message, and tell us what the login screen asks for.',
 [('Stop guessing codes', 'Repeated tries can lock the account further.'),
  ('Look for the revert email', 'Instagram sends a message when security settings change. It may offer a way back.'),
  ('Use the selfie route', 'The hacked-account flow can verify you without a code.')],
 [S('What the hacker did', 'Two-factor changes usually come with other edits: a new email, a new phone, or a new password. Each sets a different obstacle.',
    ul(['The code prompt now goes to a number you do not own.', 'Backup codes may have been generated by the hacker.', 'A new email address may have been attached.'])),
  S('What to try', ol(['Search your inbox and spam for messages about a changed security setting.', 'Open the revert link, if there is one, from the original email.', 'On the login screen use the help option for a hacked account.', 'Complete the video selfie steps in good light and wait for a reply.']),
    'Send us what you see at each step if it stops.')],
 [('Can the hacker be locked out?', 'Sometimes, through the recovery route, if Instagram confirms you are the owner.'),
  ('Can the code be skipped?', 'No. There are only official routes, and they depend on verifying you.'),
  ('What if the revert link has expired?', 'Use the hacked-account help flow instead and mention the dates.')],
 ['People who see a code prompt they cannot satisfy.', 'Owners who find backup codes in the settings that they did not create.', 'Business accounts under attack.'])

page('instagram-hacked-username-changed-by-hacker', F, 'Instagram Hacked, Username Changed by the Hacker',
 'A hacker changed your Instagram username and you cannot find your account? How to check the old handle, recover access and avoid losing the name.',
 'Hacker changed your Instagram username?', 'Username changed by hacker',
 'Your handle may be gone from view, but the account is probably still yours to recover. Act on the name early.',
 'When a hacker renames the account, your old handle can be released for others to take. Recover access first, by the hacked-account route, then change the name back. Act on the name soon, because once someone else takes it, the options are fewer. Tell us the old handle and the new one if you can see it.',
 [('Note the old handle', 'Write it down now with the date it changed.'),
  ('Recover access first', 'The name can only be changed back after you control the account.'),
  ('Watch for the handle', 'If someone else takes it, a username claim may be an option.')],
 [S('Why the old name matters', 'Instagram releases a username once it is changed. A hacker who changes your handle may sell or abandon it, and others can register it.',
    ul(['Your old handle appears available or shows another account.', 'Links and tags to your name point nowhere.', 'The hacker may use the old name to impersonate you.'])),
  S('What to do', ol(['Use the hacked-account help flow and say that the username was changed.', 'Check old emails for a message about the username change and use any revert link.', 'Once in, change the username back if it is available.', 'If it is taken, tell us and we will look at a claim or a report for impersonation.']))],
 [('Can I get my old username back?', 'If it is available, yes, once you control the account. If someone else has it, it depends on the route.'),
  ('Does reverting the name restore my account?', 'No. Recovery of access comes first.'),
  ('Will the hacker keep my followers?', 'As long as they control the account, yes. That is why speed matters.')],
 ['Owners whose handle no longer matches their name.', 'Brands whose old handle is now different.', 'People whose followers see a changed profile.'])

page('instagram-hacked-followers-getting-scam-messages', F, 'Instagram Hacked, Followers Getting Scam Messages',
 'Your hacked Instagram account is messaging your followers with scams? How to warn people, limit the damage and recover the account.',
 'Hacked Instagram account sending scam messages?', 'Hacked account messaging followers',
 'Every hour the hacker has access, more of your followers see the scam. Here is how to limit it.',
 'When a hacker uses your account to message followers, the priority is recovery and warning people through other channels. Tell friends and customers not to click or send money, report the messages, and use the hacked-account recovery route. Do not reply to the hacker or pay anything.',
 [('Warn people elsewhere', 'Use email, a group chat or another account to tell followers to ignore the messages.'),
  ('Do not engage the hacker', 'Replying or paying does not return access.'),
  ('Start recovery now', 'The longer it runs, the more likely further flags are.')],
 [S('Common scam patterns', ul(['Requests for a small loan or gift card.', 'An investment or crypto offer from someone who normally does not post about it.', 'A link to a fake login page that spreads the hack.', 'A prize or giveaway that asks for details.']),
    'Anyone who clicked should change their own passwords.'),
  S('What to do', ol(['Post a warning from another channel and ask people to report the messages.', 'Check the email on the account for security alerts and use any revert link.', 'Use the hacked-account recovery flow and follow the selfie steps.', 'Contact us with what you can still see.']))],
 [('Could my account be suspended for what the hacker sent?', 'It can be flagged. Explain in the appeal that you were hacked and did not send the messages.'),
  ('Should I delete the account?', 'No. Deleting can make recovery harder.'),
  ('Should I tell followers to report?', 'Yes, they can report the messages as scams, which helps flag the activity.')],
 ['Creators whose followers are being targeted.', 'Shops that fear losing customers.', 'People who see strange posts and stories.'])

page('instagram-hacked-no-login-link-in-email', F, 'Instagram Hacked and No Login Link Arrives',
 'You asked Instagram for a login link and nothing arrives, because the email or phone on the account was changed? What to check and what to try.',
 'Instagram login link never arrives after a hack?', 'No login link after a hack',
 'If the link never comes, the contact details were probably changed. That points to a specific recovery route.',
 'If Instagram’s login link or code never reaches you, the email or phone on the account was probably changed by the hacker. Look for a message about the change in your inbox, then use the hacked-account route and its video selfie instead of the reset link, which now goes to the wrong place.',
 [('Search for the change alert', 'Instagram emails the old address when the email is changed.'),
  ('Do not keep requesting links', 'They go to the hacker’s address.'),
  ('Use the selfie route', 'It does not depend on the email.')],
 [S('Why the link is missing', ul(['The email on the account was replaced.', 'The phone number was removed or swapped.', 'The old address filters out Instagram messages.', 'A login on a new device triggered a hold.'])),
  S('What to try', ol(['Search the old email for Instagram messages dated around the hack.', 'If a revert link is there, use it straight away.', 'Otherwise open the help flow for a hacked account on the login screen.', 'Follow the video selfie steps and keep your screenshots.']))],
 [('How do I know the email was changed?', 'A security email may exist. If not, the login prompt shows a masked address that is not yours.'),
  ('Can the hacker see my reset link?', 'If it goes to their address, yes. That is why you should not keep requesting them.'),
  ('What if I never had a security email?', 'Spam folders or old addresses may hold it. Tell us what you find.')],
 ['People whose reset emails do not come.', 'Owners who see an unfamiliar masked address.', 'Anyone who lost their phone number.'])

page('instagram-hacked-after-phishing-dm-link', F, 'Instagram Hacked After Clicking a Phishing Link',
 'You clicked a link in an Instagram DM and then lost access? How these phishing pages work, what to change first and how recovery usually goes.',
 'Instagram hacked after a phishing message?', 'Hacked after phishing link',
 'A message saying your account will be removed is often a trap. If you entered your login, here is what to do.',
 'Phishing messages copy Instagram’s style and send you to a fake login page, which collects your username and password. If you entered them, change the password on the real app right away if you still can, and also the email password. Then use the hacked-account recovery route if access is already gone.',
 [('Change passwords first', 'Instagram and then the email, from a device you trust.'),
  ('Log out all devices', 'Do this from the security settings once you are back in.'),
  ('Warn your contacts', 'The hacker may reuse your account to send the same message.')],
 [S('How the trap works', ul(['A DM or email says you broke copyright, or that your account will be removed.', 'It asks you to log in or verify by a link.', 'The page looks real but sends your login to the attacker.', 'The attacker then logs in and changes your settings.']),
    'Instagram does not ask you to log in through a link from a stranger.'),
  S('What to do', ol(['If you can still log in, change the password and log out other sessions.', 'Change the email password too, if the same password is reused anywhere.', 'If access is gone, use the hacked-account help flow and the selfie steps.', 'Tell your followers to ignore messages from your account.']))],
 [('Does Instagram send removal warnings by DM?', 'No. Official notices are in the app’s Account Status and in emails from Instagram’s own domain.'),
  ('Can I prevent this again?', 'Turn on two-factor, use a password manager, and never log in through a link in a message.'),
  ('What if I used the same password elsewhere?', 'Change it everywhere, starting with the email account.')],
 ['People who entered a password on a fake page.', 'Creators and shops that get many DMs.', 'Anyone fearing they were phished.'])

page('instagram-hacked-and-deleted-by-hacker', F, 'Instagram Hacked and the Account Was Deleted',
 'A hacker deleted your Instagram account? What deletion means, whether recovery is still possible and which details to collect straight away.',
 'Hacker deleted your Instagram account?', 'Account deleted by a hacker',
 'Deleted by someone else is not the same as deleted by you. The details decide what is possible.',
 'When a hacker deletes an Instagram account, there may still be a window in which the account can be restored, but it is not open for long and not always available. Act straight away: check your email for deletion messages, use the hacked-account route and tell us the exact dates.',
 [('Check email for the notice', 'A deletion message shows the date and may include a link.'),
  ('Use the hacked route', 'Say plainly that you did not delete it.'),
  ('Act without delay', 'Delay narrows the options.')],
 [S('Deleted or disabled?', 'A deleted account and a temporarily disabled one are treated differently. The wording on the login screen tells you which it is.',
    ul(['Temporarily disabled accounts can be reactivated by logging in.', 'Deleted accounts may be in a pending state for a limited period.', 'Fully deleted accounts cannot be restored.'])),
  S('What to do', ol(['Search your email for any message about deletion or a request to delete.', 'Try logging in and screenshot what appears.', 'Use the hacked-account help flow and explain the sequence of events.', 'Send us the date and the screenshots.']),
    'If the deletion has gone through completely, we will tell you honestly that there is likely nothing to restore.')],
 [('How long do I have?', 'It depends on the state of the account. We cannot say. Check the login screen and email dates now.'),
  ('Does it matter that the hacker did it?', 'Yes. Say clearly that you did not request it.'),
  ('Can Unbanz undo a deletion?', 'No. We help with the request and the details. Instagram decides.')],
 ['People whose profile shows no longer available.', 'Owners with a deletion email they did not request.', 'Business accounts that were wiped.'])

page('instagram-hacked-business-account-with-ads-running', F, 'Hacked Instagram Business Account Running Ads',
 'A hacker is running ads from your Instagram business account or ad account? How to stop spend, secure the assets and start recovery in the right order.',
 'Hacked Instagram business account running ads?', 'Hacked business account with ads',
 'Ads on a hacked account mean money leaving and flags building. The order of your actions matters here.',
 'If a hacker runs ads through your business account, stop the spend first: remove the payment method from the ad account in Meta Business settings, or contact your bank about the card. Then secure the Facebook login, remove unknown admins, and start account recovery. Keep records of the charges.',
 [('Stop the spend', 'Remove the payment method or ask your bank to block further charges.'),
  ('Remove unknown admins', 'In business settings, check people and assets.'),
  ('Keep records', 'Screenshots of ads and charges support later requests.')],
 [S('What to check in Meta settings', ul(['The list of people with access to the ad account and the business portfolio.', 'Connected pages and Instagram accounts.', 'Payment methods and recent charges.', 'Active campaigns and who created them.']),
    'If you cannot log in to the Facebook profile behind it, treat it as a Facebook recovery too.'),
  S('What to do first', ol(['Block the card through your bank if you cannot remove it yourself.', 'Secure the email and the Facebook login, if you still have access.', 'Remove unknown users and pause campaigns.', 'Use the hacked-account route for the Instagram account, and tell us what has been charged.']),
    'Ad accounts used for fraud can be disabled. If that happens, our ad account pages cover the appeal.')],
 [('Will Meta reimburse the charges?', 'That is between you, your bank and Meta’s billing process. We cannot say how it will go.'),
  ('Could the ad account be disabled?', 'Yes, ads placed by a hacker can lead to a restriction. Explain what happened in any appeal.'),
  ('Should I tell my customers?', 'If the ads promote something fraudulent, a short public note helps avoid confusion.')],
 ['Businesses that see unknown ads or charges.', 'Agencies that manage client accounts.', 'Anyone whose payment method is in use by someone else.'])

page('instagram-hacked-facebook-also-lost', F, 'Instagram Hacked and the Linked Facebook Is Lost Too',
 'A hacker took your Instagram and the Facebook account linked to it? How linked logins make recovery more complicated and where to start.',
 'Instagram and linked Facebook both hacked?', 'Instagram and Facebook both hacked',
 'When two accounts are linked, a hacker often takes both. Recovery needs a plan that covers each.',
 'If both the Instagram and the Facebook account tied to it are gone, start from the email address, which is usually the common point. Secure it first. Then recover Facebook, since many of the account settings link back to it, and use the hacked-account route for Instagram. Tell us which one you can still see.',
 [('Secure the email', 'It is the common link between both accounts.'),
  ('Do Facebook early', 'Business tools and logins may depend on it.'),
  ('Keep a record', 'Dates and screenshots for both help each request.')],
 [S('Why one hack becomes two', ul(['Instagram was set up with the Facebook login.', 'The same email and password were used for both.', 'A hacker used one account to reset the other.', 'The Instagram account is a business one connected to a Facebook Page.']),
    'Page and ad account access can be lost with the profile.'),
  S('Order of work', ol(['Secure the email account and change its password.', 'Start Facebook recovery with the official hacked-account flow.', 'Start Instagram recovery in parallel with the selfie flow.', 'Write to us with a short timeline and the screenshots of both.']))],
 [('Which should I recover first?', 'The email, then Facebook, then Instagram. Do them in parallel where you can.'),
  ('Will recovering Facebook restore Instagram?', 'Not on its own. Each account has its own recovery route.'),
  ('What if I have a business Page?', 'Pages and ad accounts have their own roles. Check who has admin access, and tell us what you can no longer see.')],
 ['People who see both accounts logged out.', 'Page admins who use Instagram for marketing.', 'Owners who linked the two with one login.'])

page('instagram-hacked-phone-number-removed', F, 'Instagram Hacked and Your Phone Number Was Removed',
 'The phone number was removed or replaced on your Instagram after a hack, possibly after a SIM swap? How to check and which routes are still open.',
 'Phone number removed from your hacked Instagram?', 'Phone number removed after hack',
 'Once the phone number is gone, SMS codes stop reaching you. These are the checks to make and the routes left.',
 'When a hacker removes or replaces the phone number on the account, text codes stop working. Check with your mobile provider whether your SIM was moved, then use the hacked-account route, which relies on a selfie instead of an SMS. Keep the dates of any strange calls, texts or signal loss.',
 [('Check your SIM', 'Sudden loss of signal can mean a SIM swap. Call your provider.'),
  ('Do not rely on SMS', 'If the number was changed, codes go elsewhere.'),
  ('Use the selfie route', 'It does not depend on the number.')],
 [S('What a SIM swap looks like', ul(['Your phone suddenly has no service for no reason.', 'You receive messages about a SIM change you did not request.', 'Several accounts fall at once.']),
    'If it applies, secure your bank and email accounts as well.'),
  S('What to do', ol(['Contact your mobile provider and ask whether your number was moved.', 'Secure the email accounts that use that phone number.', 'Use the Instagram help flow for a hacked account and complete the selfie steps.', 'Send us the dates of the signal loss and the screenshots of the login screen.']))],
 [('Can I stop this happening again?', 'Use an authenticator app instead of SMS, and ask your provider to add a PIN on the number.'),
  ('Is this common?', 'It happens often enough that providers can set extra protection. Ask yours.'),
  ('Is Unbanz able to restore the number?', 'No. We help with the Instagram recovery requests only.')],
 ['People who lost mobile service and then access.', 'Owners who used SMS as the only second step.', 'Anyone who sees the number replaced in the account.'])

page('instagram-hacker-demands-money', F, 'Hacker Demands Money to Return Your Instagram',
 'Someone holds your Instagram account and asks you to pay? Why paying does not help, how the scam works and what the real recovery routes are.',
 'Hacker wants money to give your Instagram back?', 'Hacker asking for payment',
 'This is a scam on top of a hack. Paying seldom returns the account and often brings more demands.',
 'If someone who holds your account asks for payment to return it, do not pay. Nothing says the account comes back, and it often leads to further demands. Report the messages, document them, and use the official hacked-account recovery flow. If the hacker threatens to publish private content, tell the police.',
 [('Do not pay', 'Payment seldom restores access and often leads to more demands.'),
  ('Save the messages', 'Screenshots help with reports and any police report.'),
  ('Use the official route', 'The selfie flow is the genuine way back.')],
 [S('How the demand works', ul(['The hacker keeps the account and asks for a fee.', 'Some pose as helpers who say they can restore it for money.', 'Others threaten to delete or publish content.', 'After a payment the account may not be returned.']),
    'The same applies to offers from strangers who say they can get your account back for a fee through private contacts.'),
  S('What to do', ol(['Stop replying to the person and keep the messages.', 'Report the account and messages as scams.', 'Start the hacked-account recovery flow with the selfie steps.', 'If threats are involved, contact the police and tell us what you can share.']))],
 [('Can the hacker be reported?', 'Yes. Report the messages and the profile through the app, and keep screenshots.'),
  ('Does Unbanz ask for logins or card details?', 'No. We never ask for your login or card details in messages. Beware anyone who does.'),
  ('Will recovery work after a demand?', 'The official route does not depend on what the hacker says. It depends on verifying you.')],
 ['People who received a ransom message.', 'Owners tempted by offers from strangers.', 'Anyone holding evidence they want to report.'])
